WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:06.080
The Da Vinci Surgical System is the
most advanced robot in surgery.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.408
It doesn't operate alone: it's a
slave robot that follows each move


00:00:10.408 --> 00:00:14.718
of the surgeon, enhancing precision
and removing hand tremors.


00:00:14.718 --> 00:00:20.177
The doctor works from a console,
controlling the robotic arms.

00:00:20.177 --> 00:00:25.210
They see inside the patient in 3D
and high definition, as if they were

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:30.210
inside the body. They can also view
prior images and biopsies.

00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:34.485
Even fluorescence can be used to
detect vessels and reduce bleeding.

00:00:34.485 --> 00:00:40.303
Advantages: less blood loss,
fewer complications, shorter

00:00:40.303 --> 00:00:43.813
hospital stays and a
much faster recovery.

00:00:43.813 --> 00:00:48.930
In short, Da Vinci doesn't replace
the surgeon… it empowers them.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:53.860
It's the best example of how
technology makes medicine more

00:00:53.860 --> 00:01:00.759
precise, safe and human.
Robotics is transforming surgery.